  rationale: displayed timing values are formatted with the shared latency
  formatter and carry their own ms/s unit text, so the semantic header is more
  accurate than a fixed "(ms)" header.
- ResultDetail expanded raw samples table expected "Duration (ms)" but the
  product now renders "Duration".
  classification: stale test against the shared dynamic-unit contract.
  rationale: raw duration cells are also formatted with the shared latency
  formatter and carry their own ms/s unit text.
- ResultDetail canonical summary expected exact "3,000.42" but rendered compact
  "3,000".
  classification: product-contract defect.
  rationale: Result Detail is a receipt/detail surface where exact score
